# Deployment settings of the CP-SAT Log Analyzer, read by `docker compose up`
# from a file named `.env` next to docker-compose.yml. Copy this file to `.env`
# and fill in what your deployment needs; everything here is optional and the
# app runs without it. See docs/deployment.md for the details.

# Where the "Report issue" link in the top bar points.
# ISSUE_URL=https://github.com/d-krupke/CP-SAT-Log-Analyzer/issues

# Legal pages. Operating a public website in Germany/the EU requires an imprint
# and a privacy statement; they belong to you as the operator, so the app ships
# without them. Either link to pages you already have ...
# IMPRINT_URL=https://krupke-algorithms.de/impressum
# PRIVACY_URL=https://krupke-algorithms.de/datenschutz

# ... or write them as Markdown, mount the directory (see the `volumes:` block
# in docker-compose.yml) and let the app show them in a dialog:
# IMPRINT_FILE=/legal/imprint.md
# PRIVACY_FILE=/legal/privacy.md

# Link texts, if the defaults ("Impressum", "Privacy") do not fit.
# IMPRINT_LABEL=Impressum
# PRIVACY_LABEL=Datenschutz
